  "overview_data_sha256": "71ad97b9d3acd686c3c86a791589368621717604687fce2aa553df495936cabf",
  "overview_readme_sha256": "32fc0dd81bc4742cad67bc23231c08daa7f480c0d8c2aec559e5f6c8ad951467",
  "overview_readme_text": "# Stage 27 draft: a filtered-numerator bridge through g=.112\n\n**DRAFT, awaiting root review and freeze.** For the ordinary isotropic periodic spin-half square bilayer with unit rung exchange and equal straight intralayer exchange:\n\n- Every real `g\u2208[.11,.112]`, every integer square side `L\u22652`: unique finite-volume ground and **gap\u2265.01**.\n- Joining the old interval: every real `g\u2208[0,.112]`, every integer `L\u22652`: unique ground and **gap\u2265.0001**.\n- Separate point certificates at `.1105,.111,.112` give `.01`; their earlier `10^-6` certificates remain as weaker history.\n\nOdd sides and the positive-direction periodic multiedge convention, including L2 parallel edges, are included. This is the ordinary bilayer, not the fully frustrated model. No conclusion beyond `.112`, optimality, physical phase boundary or true-gap estimate is claimed. All stronger old nested bounds, earlier point certificates and Stage26 fixed-family diagnostics remain valid.\n\nThe independent interval acceptance is [24fa3538\u2026](../bilayer_filtered_numerator_continuous_review60/PROOF.md), full seal `24fa35384ccf138c6f65bc4c1af1b2eb9a4c718a2ecbca7901205ea9e381dd80`. Sixteen exact closed leaves of width1/8000 cover the new bridge:\n\n`I_i=[(880+i)/8000,(881+i)/8000]`, i=0,\u2026,15.\n\nThey join the previous102 closed pieces for118 pieces, with common lower bound `.0001`. The new bridge separately retains its stronger `.01`. The new proof also strengthens g=.11 itself, while preserving its earlier weaker point bound.\n\nPrevious frozen overview: Stage26, seal `39c5b54f1769ba203703e850d21423e252512604126d20cea9d6df784382f1e9`. Live Stage23 root files and separate Stage24\u201326 prepared copies are untouched. Latest remotely verified main remains Stage22 `d17eadfb655c35eb325245d8660737b761db6b28`, verified2026-10-11 06:14:45 UTC; GitHub blob approval remains blocked. This local snapshot is not a remote publication claim.\n\n## Why the new physical numerator escapes the old fixed-family exclusions\n\nLet \u03c8 be the normalized old57D numerator trial, `\u03bc(g)=\u3008\u03c8,H\u2032(g)\u03c8\u3009`, and `r(g)=(H\u2032(g)\u2212\u03bc(g))\u03c8`. The64-rung /128-spin numerator has\n\n`H\u2032(g)=H+48=Q+(g/2)A`.\n\nThe trial has even triplet sectors q\u22646; the residual has q\u22648. The new implicit physical state is proportional to `\u03c8\u2212\u03c4r(g)`. Its fixed-g plane has dimension at most2; adjoining its residual to the old57D preparation family gives dimension at most58. Only one numerator trial contribution is retained. The full physical Hilbert dimension remains `2^128`; none of these dimensions is an MPS bond dimension.\n\nThe earlier57D and joint fixed2D/57D exclusions remain true: the new residual direction enlarges that old numerator family. No full physical q8 vector needs to be stored. The exact filtered norm is not computed. It is `1+\u03c4\u00b2v(g)` for the normalized seed, where `v(g)=||r(g)||\u00b2` is the **unknown true complete variance**.\n\n### A lower bound on variance, not a completed second moment\n\nThe independent [analytic review](../bilayer_variance_lower_filter_analytic_review/PROOF_REVIEW.md), seal `84bf483e52892482998f7c8e3c138b373421e72ab3d338d05ce97c8a70677994`, proves `[C,C\u2020]\u2265216` on q6 for the simple degree-four8\u00d78 rung graph. Here C\u2020 is the unscaled pair-creation block of A; the physical coefficient is `g/2`, not g.\n\nWith the old exact norm n, q6 raw norm w and the accepted28D q4 projection h, the q8 contribution gives\n\n`v(g)\u2265\u03bag\u00b2`, where `\u03ba=(216w+h)/(4n)>0`.\n\nThe discrete-point numerical review also checks the nonnegative57D projected residual, whose q\u22646 support is orthogonal to q8, and can add it without double counting. The uniform proof deliberately drops that optional contribution: it never claims a convex quadratic minimum follows from checking endpoints.\n\nThese quantities are variance **lower bounds**, not the actual variance or a complete64-rung H\u00b2 matrix. No full-support contraction or new complete numerator second-moment calculation ran. The old exact n is known; that does not make the new filtered norm known.\n\n### Uniform descent with the true norm retained\n\nThe compressed q\u22648 expectation is bounded by a5\u00d75 Jacobi comparison matrix. A common rational upper is `R*=11382382495463/10^12`. Positive LDL pivots at b*=.112, together with nonnegative entrywise domination and replacement of vectors by absolute values, give the uniform expectation upper. This is not a Loewner assertion `J(b*)\u2212J(g)\u22650`, and not a full-Hilbert spectral support upper. Any H\u2032r component at q10 is orthogonal to r in the needed expectation.\n\nOn a closed leaf[a,b], the proof uses `s=\u03baa\u00b2`, affine \u03bc(g), `Cmax=R*\u2212min(\u03bc(a),\u03bc(b))`, and constant positive \u03b4,\u03c4 satisfying `\u03c4=\u03b4/s<1/Cmax` and `\u03b4(Cmax+\u03b4)\u2264s`. Then\n\n`Rayleigh(\u03c8\u2212\u03c4r(g)) \u2264 \u03bc(g)\u2212v(g)(2\u03c4\u2212Cmax\u03c4\u00b2)/(1+\u03c4\u00b2v(g)) \u2264 \u03bc(g)\u2212\u03b4`.\n\nThe second comparison uses monotonicity in the unknown `v(g)\u2265s`. It does not replace the physical norm by `1+\u03c4\u00b2s`. The resulting numerator upper `\u03bc(g)\u2212\u03b4` is affine and valid for every real g in the closed leaf, not just its endpoints.\n\n## Accepted point and interval checks\n\nThe [numerical filter review](../bilayer_numerator_q8_variance_lower_review24/PROOF.md), seal `8033d465f4526dcf1ece20985f624d3d8744906e53b9cf455ef1998f070fd73b`, independently verifies the filter arithmetic, exact physical denominator seeds,22 finite windows and a tail per point. It promotes the attained sufficient targets to actual all-size gaps `10^-6` at `.1105,.111,.112`. At `.115` this filter is insufficient for its declared target; that is not a physical exclusion.\n\nThe [stronger point review](../bilayer_filtered_numerator_point_closure_review12/PROOF.md), seal `1b3066ecb1a0820632e9f17c3e5ec9fe02434de96902739e4d23830b5c1ac9ee`, uses the strongest physical filter endpoints and the predeclared reporting levels. It accepts `.01` at all three points, with4/4/5 finite windows and terminal sides64/64/128. These point statements alone do not interpolate a coupling interval.\n\nThe separate uniform bridge review checks all16 leaves analytically and with directed arithmetic. Ground32 coefficients are fixed on each leaf: I00\u2013I03 use the `.1105` witness, I04\u2013I07 the `.111` witness, and I08\u2013I15 the `.112` witness. The fixed basis remains `span{\u03c8,T0\u03c8}`, `T0=200Q+11A`; its second vector is not redefined as H(g)\u03c8. Full G,K(g),J(g) are used, with no extra division by200 or projected substitution `J=KG^-1K`.\n\nFour ground variance PSD forms plus48 odd-mode forms make52 full variance checks. Convex variances and concave analytic-reference-minus-affine-mean functions justify whole-leaf extrema. Complete odd modes, their spin multiplicity, full bosonic tails and the full-sector second-level count remain. The r2 cutoff is the second level in the relevant full invariant sector, not the full-Hilbert second energy or a projected Ritz surrogate. Retained counts remain49,97,1.\n\nIndependent640-bit directed exponentials and exact downward-grid recurrences check67 finite windows and16 tails. I00\u2013I12 use4 windows and tail64; I13\u2013I15 use5 windows and tail128. L2\u20137 use the separately accepted short bridge, gap `.050426624396` over[0,.15], which contains the entire extension. The minimum over short sizes, every finite window and each infinite tail yields `.01`. All integer sides, including odd ones, are covered.\n\nThe16 closed leaves meet exactly, including the witness changes at `.1105` and `.111`. No equality of adjacent witness vectors is required. The old right endpoint `.11` equals the new left endpoint exactly, so the118-piece join proves[0,.112]/.0001. No endpoint-gap interpolation, adaptive subdivision or new parameter search is used.\n\n## Failed startups, resource reservations and preserved exceptions\n\n| Phase | Reserved CPU | Result |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Three failed filter startups |20+20+20|All failed before science; all60 retained|\n| Successful filter producer and numerical review |24+24|PASS; cumulative108|\n| Stronger-point producer and review |12+12|PASS; cumulative132|\n| Uniform pilot, cover and review |24+36+60|PASS; cumulative252|\n\nThe initial failures were: Python bootstrap under inheritedAS32; inability to raise inherited hard CPU4 to15 before science; parent json-import ENOMEM underAS32 before children. Attempts2/3 have no measured CPU receipts. Their actual CPU remains unknown, not zero. Authoritative raw snapshots and hashes are inside producer `3322ce\u2026/FAILED_STARTUPS.json` and `failed_startup_snapshots`; no independent whole-directory seal is invented for the old failed working directories. Directly reviewed historical source files are pinned individually.\n\nThe full252 no-refund reservation chain is retained. Older interval160, older point72, Stage26 diagnostic248, complete scientific-review204 and physical-production22983 remain separate histories. Ancillary preparation/sealing is conservatively charged but not individually metered. The earlier scalar-target worker20.407048>20 component failure remains despite aggregate20.730588<24. Original whole-moment production remains **FAILED_ACCOUNTING_TERMINAL**, with unknown exception and missing receipts unresolved. Mathematical acceptance does not repair those records.\n\n## Documentary deliverables and boundary\n\n- [Filter endpoints](stage27_filter_endpoints.csv): all four tested g and four variance-lower variants; `.115` nonpromotion retained\n- [Six point records](stage27_point_certificates.csv): weaker10^-6 and stronger.01 separately\n- [16 closed interval leaves](stage27_interval_pieces.csv) and [bridge/join summaries](stage27_interval_summary.csv)\n- [Proof scope](stage27_proof_scope.csv), [accounting](stage27_accounting.csv), [failed startups](stage27_failed_startups.csv)\n- [All381 main certificate records](stage27_all_certificates.csv), preserving all357 inherited rows\n- [New bridge figure](stage27_filtered_bridge.png), also [PDF](stage27_filtered_bridge.pdf)\n\nOrdinary code, proof and manifest files remain ordinary repository files. The prior44 exact-member archive descriptors and10,205 transport mappings are reused unchanged. Metadata/source equality, manifest replay, exact coverage, corruption guards and byte-identical rendering are overview checks only; no physical kernel or scientific bootstrap replay runs here. The existing scientific one-use scripts retain their separate authority.\n\nThe newer stronger[.108,.11] bridge plan and3D Krylov source-only work are excluded. Separate Stage27 root copies will be prepared, preserving all older pins. Latest user report:2026-10-11 11:41:35 UTC; next fixed report13:15 UTC. Scientific hard cutoff remains2026-10-14 00:00 UTC /October13 20:00 EDT.\n",
  "new_rows_exact": [
